9:### Segment binding (guards.md command 5, pre-build leg)
13:ASR line record (asr-segments.json, faster-whisper fa): 
17:- L4 79.48–81.58 «از باباش قرض گرفته بود» (5 words; ASR «قرز» corrected to قرض per digest's frame-verified correction practice)
19:### Motion census (A10.3) — frames extracted by the builder, viewed firsthand
22:### Mechanics + sub-beats (firsthand from census frames + evidence frames)
27:5. **Line lifecycle:** a line appears at its speech onset (all dim except the first word brightening), sweeps to fully white at its last word, holds fully-lit briefly (f-77.5: L2 fully white 0.5 s after its ASR end, before L3's chunk dominates), and is replaced by the next line at the next onset. One line owns the band at a time (Owner Cure 2 phase exclusivity applies by analogy).
30:### Variables (§1.3 extraction)
33:### Schedule basis (A7)
34:**segment-anchored** — line onsets/ends sit at their ASR-measured source times, re-based to segment t=0 by CONFIG segmentStartMs (73500). Per-word onsets inside a line are an **allocation**: proportional to word character length across the line's measured interval (ASR carries no word-level timings; the allocation is named here and in CONFIG derivation code, never presented as measured).
36:### Census-anchor mapping (A10.2)
